      en: "War Remnants Museum is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Vietnam. A museum in Ho Chi Minh City which exhibits related to the First Indochina War and the Vietnam War. Contains US military vehicles and weaponry. Documents the atrocities of war. One of the most popular attractions in the city. This site holds particular significance in the history of Vietnam, from imperial dynasties to the French colonial era. Like many notable places in Vietnam, it combines regional character with the legacy of a millennia-old civilization and the French colonial era. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Vietnam — from the Mekong Delta and Ha Long Bay to the terraced rice fields.",
